//! The mini USB B receptacle of Shenzhen Shouhan Technology, MINI 5PTP (LCSC C2681563): the USB1
//! of ORBIT. Surface mount, right angle, five contacts, a shell that is soldered at four pads
//! and two locating holes. The author's schematic calls it `USB Connector`.
//!
//! The maker's approval sheet (part number written `MINI 5PTP-GZ`, three pages, the drawing
//! dated 2020.8.24) draws the part and a RECOMMENDED PCB LAYOUT but numbers neither the
//! contacts nor the shell. The numbers are ORBIT's: contacts 1 to 5 as the board's USB nets
//! say (VBUS, D-, D+, an unconnected ID, GND), and the shell on pads 6 to 9, which the board
//! carries. The pin names are the USB signals' own, not the maker's. Contact current 1 A,
//! 30 V DC (page 2 and the drawing).

import std::parts::connector::Connector

/// A mini USB B receptacle, 5 contacts, SMT. `.vbus` and `.gnd` are the power contacts, `.id`
/// is the ID contact (not connected on a device), `.shield` is the metal shell, four pads that
/// are one pin. The two locating holes have no pad number and are not in the pin table.
part ShouHanMini5ptp provides Connector {
    pins {
        //  pin        kind           name       pads
        .vbus     power         "VBUS"     "1"
        .dm       bidirectional "D-"       "2"
        .dp       bidirectional "D+"       "3"
        .id       passive       "ID"       "4"
        .gnd      power         "GND"      "5"
        .shield   passive       "SHIELD"   "6" "7" "8" "9"
    }

    .mpn: String
    .package: Package
    catalog usb_mini_b by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
